<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rostislav Mikhailovich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1262">1262</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rostislav Mikhailovich was a Rus prince, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-of-chernigov">Michael of Chernigov</a>, who briefly held Halych before losing it to Daniel of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>. He married a daughter of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bela-iv-of-hungary">Béla IV of Hungary</a> and around 1247 received the banate of Macsó south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a>, along with Bosnian lands, which he held as a Hungarian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> and frontier lord until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rostislav-mikhailovich.jpg" alt="Rostislav Mikhailovich" width="320" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Goran tek-en, following request by and knowledge from Veverve · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kievan_Rus_in_1237_(en).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
